@NODE main "Fixture -- the md2guide mapping"
@{b}@{u}Fixture -- the md2guide mapping@{uu}@{ub}

The golden fixture of tools/docs/md2guide.lisp: one instance of every
Markdown construct the converter supports, converted by make test and
compared byte-for-byte with fixture.guide (see specs/amigaguide-docs.md).
Everything before the first level-2 heading is the body of the main node.

    @{b}Note:@{ub} a block quote is indented four columns, and the bold lead keeps
    its bold. A link inside it works: @{"Tables" LINK "tables"}.

- @{b}Package:@{ub} FIXTURE (uses CL)
- A bullet item long enough to be re-flowed onto a second line, with a
  hanging indent, inline code, @{i}italic@{ui} and @{b}bold@{ub} text, and a link to @{"Other" LINK "other.guide/main"}.
  - A nested item, also long enough to wrap onto a second line with its own
    hanging indent two columns deeper.
  - Another nested item.
- Back at the top level.

1. An ordered item.
2. Another, with a link to a @{"section of the other file" LINK "other.guide/second-section"}.
3. A link into a file one directory below, @{"Child" LINK "sub/child.guide/below"}, which links back up.

@{b}Contents@{ub}

  @{" Inline markup " LINK "inline-markup"}
  @{" Characters " LINK "characters"}
  @{" Tables " LINK "tables"}
  @{" Code " LINK "code"}
    @{" A level-3 section " LINK "a-level-3-section"}
    @{" Duplicate " LINK "duplicate"}
    @{" Duplicate " LINK "duplicate-1"}
  @{" After a rule " LINK "after-a-rule"}
@ENDNODE

@NODE inline-markup "Inline markup"
@{b}@{u}Inline markup@{uu}@{ub}

Bold with @{b}two stars@{ub}, italic with @{i}one star@{ui}, nested @{i}italic with @{b}bold@{ub} inside@{ui},
code with *stars* and [brackets], a literal 5 * 3, a literal [bracketed]
word, double backticks with a ` inside, and escapes: *not italic*, `not
code`, a_b. A link whose text is its target: @{"other.md" LINK "other.guide/main"}; links that stay text:
a URL (https://example.org/path), a file that is not converted (../foo.md),
a directory (examples/), and the @{"title of this file" LINK "main"}. AmigaGuide specials in
text: an \@ sign, a \\ backslash, an \@{ brace, and a "double-quoted" phrase in
a link label: @{"see 'Tables'" LINK "tables"}.

An image on its own: @{i}The alt text of an image@{ui}, and a badge (an image inside
a link, dropped): .
@ENDNODE

@NODE characters "Characters"
@{b}@{u}Characters@{uu}@{ub}

Mapped: em--dash, en-dash, ellipsis..., arrows -> <- <-> <->, comparisons >=
<= == /=, quotes "double" and 'single', a non-breaking space, and a :-)
face. Latin-1 passes through: § × ä ö ü ß é.
@ENDNODE

@NODE tables "Tables"
@{b}@{u}Tables@{uu}@{ub}

@{b}(socket-listen port &optional loopback)@{ub}  [function]
    Open a listening server socket on a port (port 0 picks a free one;
    loopback non-nil binds 127.0.0.1 only)

@{b}*verbose*@{ub}  [variable]
    A literal pipe: a | b; @{b}bold@{ub} and a @{"link" LINK "code"} in a cell

@{b}(quiet)@{ub}  [macro]

@{b}--heap SIZE@{ub}
    Heap size
    Default: 4M

@{b}--no-image@{ub}
    Boot from the FASLs

@{b}EXT@{ub}
    Prefix: ext:
    Doc: @{"ext.md" LINK "other.guide/main"}
@ENDNODE

